   "name": "Curve evaluation",
   "workload": "24,000,000 interpolations across the curve set",
   "baseline": "CPU: evaluate the spline, one point at a time",
   "note": "Pure curve evaluation, with no instrument around it. The presampled lanes do not evaluate the curve at all: it is sampled onto 727 points once and everything after that is a lookup plus a linear step between neighbours. That is the same trade as precomputing daily discount factors, only much coarser, and the accuracy table below is what it costs. 727 points across 50 years is roughly one sample every 25 days.",
